ange there ishiki  tells koji  that he already served his purpose by  pulling him out of jigen  and making him reincarnate but koji  doesn't want to believe it  it seems like he views amado as his  friend and he doesn't even want to  consider the possibility that he lied to  him or tricked him  and the whole clone thing raises its own  philosophical questions  just as it did in pokemon the first  movie does a clone's life have less  value  and is it more dispensable than a  human's life even if the clone can feel  all of our human emotions because koji  is jiraya's clone  it's easy for us to view him as less  important than jariah but he has his own  complex life and sense of identity just  like any human  here's proof of that since he can  blindly trust in friendship  and feel betrayed very human traits  indeed then  ishiki being the cruel villain he is  tries to go after koji's sense of  identity  we all have a story or narrative that we  tell ourselves about ourselves and  seemingly koji thought of himself as a  heroic shinobi tool but ishiki says he  was nothing like that  but a mere pitiful sacrificial pawn here  he's not just dominating him physically  he's seriously messing with him on a  psychological level  we luckily get to see koji enter sage  mode which is pretty cool  he won't give up that easily whether his  own identity and existence  is in question or not again i respect  koji and i'm glad we got him in the  story i don't think it takes anything  away from jiraiya  rather it gives us a new character that  jaraya fans would probably enjoy  and that's coming from a guy whose  favorite character is jiraiya  we jump to amado who as i mentioned  before  has got to be one of the coolest  characters in boruto thus far he's not  even a ninja but he's so  calm cool and collected all the time and  even an otsutsuki  can't help but praise his intellect and  plans they agree to take in a motto and  give him some pretty reasonable terms  finally when shikamatu asks him to  disarm the bomb around his son's neck a  motto simply tells him it's a fake  it's just a decoration now i can't say i  saw this coming  but it makes perfect sense amado does  everything with a purpose  he explains how he used a real one the  one that blew up on the branch  so that they couldn't assume that the  one on chica died was fake  but he also knows that people don't want  to work and trust people  who have threatened the lives of their  children so he made sure that at the end  of the day  everyone knew that he didn't actually  threaten anyone's life  really he got the benefit without the  lasting consequences  a perfect win-win situation and he  pulled it off on shikamatu of all people  i gotta say it i find amado very  entertaining as a character we also get  some cool angles while motto is speaking  and explaining that they shouldn't rush  off to help koji  because ishiki wants kawaki so they  gotta protect him and stay close to him  at all costs  until ishiki's days run out otherwise  he'll use kawaki as a vessel and  complete his perfect reincarnation  the stakes are huge right now amato  tells them that ishiki is gonna come  and they should start evacuating the  village we know from the time skip that  we saw at the beginning of boruto that  the hidden leaf village will get  destroyed and the hokage faces too  so that actually could happen real soon  which is crazy to think about it might  get evacuated and stay destroyed for  years  before we get that final epic fight  between kawaki and boruto  and if that time skip scene is any  indication ishiki probably will get  kawaki as a vessel although there may be  a battle for control of the body within  like with naruto and kurama in the  beginning of naruto it's crazy that we  are finally starting to get crucial info  so that we can start to make more sense  of that time skip scene  for now though we get back to koji and  ishiki  koji is in sage mode and firing some  very impressive attacks  we get giant flame bombs a massive  rasengan  and more but it's no use ishiki puts a  stop to him without breaking a sweat  with the secret jutsu  daikokuten it lets him store what he  shrunk into another dimension  very kamui-esque and then summon it in a  battle at full size  he does this with pillars that take out  koji's arm and possibly his legs too  then the dude uses the opi jutsu to  summon a glass of wine  and then drink some what a mad lad he is  i do enjoy the idea of a shonen villain  just drinking some red wine  during a fight that's classy af again  ishiki brings up how koji  is skilled enough to know that he  couldn't hope to win  after the first exchange but he didn't  want to acknowledge amado's betrayal  ishiki points out how amado spotted that  weakness  using it he played koji just like he  played ishiki ishiki acknowledges that  they've been outmaneuvered by a motto  and again that's a big deal coming from  an otozuki  and here comes the moment of truth what  will happen to koji  was jiraiya brought back in a way just  to sacrifice himself again  as soon as we found out who he is i  desperately  hoped that that wouldn't happen and now  in this chapter ishiki starts to move  towards the kill  he asks koji if he has any last words  for our motto but he can't seem to hear  what the seemingly helpless koji is  saying then we get a truly epic moment  it turns out that koji was using  summoning and a giant toad pops up and  takes koji with him he makes eye contact  with ishiki  and he reverse summons away taking koji  with him  jiraiya lives in a sense and we will get  to see more of koji  i'm very very glad that they did it in  this way  because like i said last chapter it  would have sucked if he just came back  to sacrifice himself  immediately yet again as a jura fanboy  i'm glad we haven't seen the last of  koji ishiki calls koji a purposeless  stray dog which is a pretty deep  metaphor koji has no home and his one  friend betrayed him now he's also  heavily damaged but as someone who likes  his underdog  stories i look forward to seeing how  koji hopefully rises from the ashes like  a phoenix  and finds his place happiness and  purpose we'll definitely have to wait  for that  but i'm glad that there's hope at least  remember ishiki has a time limit so he's  not interested in chasing down koji  he even thinks that koji might want to  finish off a motto himself although  that's super uncharacteristic of koji  so i seriously doubt that the important  thing is he hasn't given up on life yet  ishiki in the meantime uses a space-time  ninjutsu to teleport somewhere  we jump back to naruto and boruto  arguing over whether boruto is going to  fight  naruto just says straight up that he'd  get in the way but  boruto won't give up saying that naruto  and sasuke lost against the weaker  version of ishiki  so how do they plan to win against an  even stronger version  it's a really crazy moment in boruto  when the two strongest shinobi look like  they're about to lose  sasuke mentions that he's ready to die  for the village as is naruto  he questions if borto is and borto is  speechless  he freezes proving that at this stage  he's not ready mentally or physically  for this fight  and then we learn that there is an  intruder and ishiki is just floating  over  konoha watching the ant-sized people  moving around below him this is how  fast-paced porto is  ishiki is not wasting any time we went  from an epic reveal of koji's true  identity  to a fight to koji barely escaping with  his life to ishiki immediately  teleporting to konoha  for what's sure to be the most serious  fight in boruto yet  where we'll probably see the strongest  characters go at it with their full  power  it's insane and i love it i'm on the  edge of my seat  and i'm almost shocked at how fast we're  moving here  clearly there was some potential  foreshadowing that sasuke especially and  even naruto might die  sasuke brought it up himself and if  kawaki  said after the time skip that he'll send  boruto where naruto  is that may mean that naruto is in  another dimension and that sasuke can't  rescue him  from it because sasuke is dead so there  are clues and hints right now that  sasuke specifically won't survive  but again those may be red herrings aka  fake clues  to make us worry and increased attention  i find it hard to believe that sasuke  would die  but maybe ishiki would weaken him enough  and take his eyes  so that he can't teleport through  dimensions we'll have to wait and see  anyways let me know what you thought of  this chapter and what you expect to  happen next who will die if anyone  will koji train borto during the time  skip the time skip is clearly  approaching  where boruto is going to have to mature  physically and mentally  and i'm excited to see boruto become  that very cool version of himself  that he is during the time skip scene if  you did enjoy this review and want to  keep the borato reviews coming the best  you can do is turn that like button blue  and share this video with your cultured  boruto friends  if you haven't be sure to subscribe and  this is crucial hit that notification  bell  or you will miss future boruto videos as  you impatiently wait a month for the  next chapter to drop  you can check out my growing naruto  slash portal playlist link in the  description  where i talk about the okay uchiha clan  and more  and don't forget to leave suggestions  for future video topics you're burning  up to see in the comments below  a very special thank you goes out to our  patrons over on patreon who help  make videos like this one possible first  and foremost i want to thank the one  tier patrons the ones who stand atop  all clans stephen ingrada alolan attempt  the world steelers acquire respect pate  heffa jonathan king brandon of viles  papa smurf the school bus king riser  emperor otaku ricardo martinez  thomas jones ken mono michael hyde and  jaden the vector controller  and our